.SS "void csmp::IsoparametricQuadraticTetrahedron_Test::CheckInterpolation (const \fBElement\fP< 3U > & e)"
Assigns a nodal field of variable values that then gets interpolated across the element\&. The values of this field variable are equivalent to the position ot the integration points in physical space\&. This relationship is used for the testing\&.

.PP
\fBTest\fP
.RS 4
OK SKM 3/9/14 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void csmp::IsoparametricQuadraticTetrahedron_Test::OutputFaceNormalsToVTK (const char * file, const \fBElement\fP< 3U > & e) const"
Loops over the faces of the element, collecting the (outward-pointing) face normals for display in VTK\&. Each normal is scaled by the sqrt of the element volume and placed with its origin on the barycenter of the corresponding face\&. 
.SS "void csmp::IsoparametricQuadraticTetrahedron_Test::OutputIntegrationPointsToVTK (const char * file, const \fBElement\fP< 3U > & e) const"
The integration points are coloured by number and are then output to VTK file\&. \fBPoint\fP 1=0, point2=1\&.\&.\&.n-1\&. 
.SS "void csmp::IsoparametricQuadraticTetrahedron_Test::run ()\fR [virtual]\fP"
Running the tests:

.PP
.IP "1." 4
Correct representation of element in physical space (node numbering and VTK output)
.IP "2." 4
Correct location of integration points
.IP "3." 4
Interpolation functions
.IP "  \(bu" 4
must be 1 at their node and 0 everywhere else
.IP "  \(bu" 4
their sum should be 1 at any point inside of element
.PP

.IP "4." 4
Interpolation function derivatives
.IP "  \(bu" 4
correct location (consistency with interpolation functions)
.IP "  \(bu" 4
correct orientation in parametric space
.IP "  \(bu" 4
correct orientation in physical space
.PP

.IP "5." 4
Jacobian transformation
.IP "  \(bu" 4
all scaling parameters should be one for an element in physical space with same coordinates as in parametric space
.IP "  \(bu" 4
lower to higher dim Jacobians
.IP "  \(bu" 4
efficiency of Jacobian calculations
.PP

.IP "6." 4
Volume correctness in parametric and physical space
.IP "7." 4
Interpolation of integration point values to nodes 
.PP

.PP
Implements \fBcsmp::Test\fP\&.
